00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:30.000
Time also is on the wing.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.000
there are not enough hours or days or weeks in the year to do the job.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:39.270
The razor's edge of time has cut distances to ribbons,

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:43.380
and continental and cultural interfaces that were once safely remote

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:46.460
are now within a packed lunch range of one another.

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:52.240
Nowhere is this better realized than at Operations Control, Headquarters Commander,

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:56.840
Anti-Submarine Warfare Force Pacific, Fort Island, Pearl Harbor.

00:07:56.840 --> 00:08:00.000
Here on one great board,

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:09.020
The entire Pacific Ocean, and the positions and movements of infinite numbers of bacteria-sized ships are studied as through a microscope.

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:13.280
Military ships, friendly ships, others.

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:18.210
In an ocean area representing more than 65 million square miles,

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:24.770
a submarine contact has been duly noted and will be dealt with during the morning high-level briefing.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:29.830
Just before sunrise this morning, a P-3A returning from an extended-range Delta flight

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:37.280
a radar contact position shown. One submarine contact in a tridimensional

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:42.960
arena larger than all the other oceans of the world combined. Whose responsibility is

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:49.870
it? In anti-submarine warfare, any ASW problem becomes everyone's problem.

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:55.160
As you will note, the area, datum area, is approximately 100 miles from the

00:08:55.160 --> 00:09:00.000
exercise area where we now have the ASW carrier and five destroyers conduct

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:04.500
their operational readiness evaluation. It has been confirmed that this contact is

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:09.600
not a friendly submarine. Not a friendly submarine means that it is not a US

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:14.920
submarine or one of our allies. Its position and course, taking it closer to

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:20.540
an ASW exercise area, suggests that it has come to watch and perhaps to learn

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:24.740
something of our ASW capabilities.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:41.190
This ASW carrier, the USS Yorktown, CBS 10, the famous fighting lady of World War II,

00:09:41.610 --> 00:09:47.600
is flagship for an ASW operational readiness evaluation that has been taking place for several days now.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:54.230
Heart and brain of the operation is the Combat Information Center.

00:09:55.640 --> 00:10:00.000
Eyes and ears and extensions of these probe a void.

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:07.910
From here, the fight for a free tomorrow is being directed and rehearsed blindfolded.

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:13.350
Foxes, for these ASW hounds, are several of our own submarines.

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:23.400
Their mission is to penetrate the ASW exercise area without detection or interception

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:28.710
and simulate sinking as many of our surface ships as possible while avoiding being sunk.

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:29.700
In turn,

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:41.270
silence is a submarine's great armor and her weapon is surprise mark 1800 but to be truly

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:49.400
effective she must move and movement pierces her armor 150 feet

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:14.480
Little destroyers have big ears, and they can go very deep at times and listen beyond the impenetrable layers of temperature barriers that often reflect or destroy undersea sounds.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:27.620
There are a wide variety of ears in ASW. Some transmit their information over a closed circuit.

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:37.650
Others are cast adrift in predetermined patterns to broadcast whatever they hear.

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:46.270
Sooner or later, that certain word gets back to ASW Group Combat Information Center.

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:49.750
Possible submarine contact.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:16.000
close in. Among them they carry a wide range of effective ASW weapons. The primary

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:30.000
ASW weapon is the torpedo. It also can be delivered by rocket to an area far

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:53.320
a firing ship or airdrop from a plane or helicopter or it may be borne long distances by a drone

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:58.840
remote controlled helicopter called dash to be dropped wherever the target is suspected to be

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:14.030
Another ASW weapon system fires a multitude of small depth bombs

00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:29.160
to clear the sea of any submersibles that might lie ahead of the ship.

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:33.040
in use for the Navy since 1952,

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:38.970
can still deliver a lethal punch to a lurking submarine.

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:44.590
Playing an important role in the Navy's systems integration approach to ASW

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:47.300
is the land-based Orion,

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:51.720
and herein is the key to the ASW group effectiveness

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:56.830
in carrying out the four major steps of anti-submarine warfare:

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:57.920
Detect...

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:00.000
"VP, scope, mark, zero,

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:02.590
7-3, 190 miles.

00:14:02.590 --> 00:14:03.930
Classify.

00:14:03.930 --> 00:14:07.640
Man, man, man.

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:11.090
Localize.

00:14:11.090 --> 00:14:17.010
And kill.

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:29.510
The Orion can carry over one ton of detection gear,

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:42.250
and up to three tons of ASW ordnance. She can go further and remain at the scene longer

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:49.430
than any other ASW aircraft, but she represents only part of the complete answer to the submarine

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:55.520
problem. Carrier-based, fixed-wing aircraft and

00:14:55.520 --> 00:15:00.000
helicopters provide great infighting and staying power once they have been brought to

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:07.740
the scene of the action. A destroyer, once it has arrived in a contact area, can

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:14.980
remain on the scene the longest in almost any kind of weather, can probe the

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:20.040
depths with a variable depth sonar capable of detecting the proverbial

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:26.560
needle in a liquid haystack, and can deliver more firepower per pound displaced

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:28.800
than any other ship afloat.

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:49.020
All systems and vehicles work as a team, but destroyers get thirsty and in time must be refueled at sea.

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:59.890
These birds must return to the mother ship, the big ones back to land.

00:16:07.390 --> 00:16:15.120
transplant eight has been relieved on station and is almost home. Her relief

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:19.120
continues the uninterrupted search in the contact area for the elusive

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:26.600
submarine. Continuing pressure is the heart of ASW tactics and the bane of the

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:30.000
sub skippers, especially in the air-breathing snorkel

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:41.960
A submarine is the greatest mobile listening platform there is.

