00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:53.800
Good afternoon, men.

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:54.820
This is the captain.

00:20:54.820 --> 00:21:00.000
Our operational readiness evaluation took an unexpected turn this morning.

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:08.830
morning at approximately 10:00 when Commander ASW Group 3 aboard Yorktown was notified by CTF-30

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:15.300
of the presence of an unidentified submarine contact northeast of our exercise area.

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:22.160
At approximately 12:18, one of our own submarines established contact with the intruder

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:30.000
while lying silent in the northeast sector of our exercise area. Commander ASW Group 3

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:35.200
was informed by our own submarine of the intruders estimated range and barrier.

00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:42.750
It has been decided to detach several destroyers and aircraft from our present

00:21:42.750 --> 00:21:47.930
exercise and assign them to the mission of relocating the unidentified

00:21:47.930 --> 00:21:55.990
submarine contact and track... We'll go to area x-ray echo, IFR altitude 2,000 feet.

00:21:55.990 --> 00:22:00.000
3-7, Mr. Helland... A line between a hot and cold war.

00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:04.940
is too thin to even cast a shadow.

00:22:04.940 --> 00:22:09.830
These men must always know which side of that lion they are operating on.

00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:14.710
The visiting unidentified submarine has every legal right to be where it is,

00:22:14.710 --> 00:22:17.320
regardless of the true purpose behind the visit.

00:23:14.360 --> 00:23:18.740
Transplant 1 has been searching in that area since arriving on station.

00:23:18.740 --> 00:23:22.500
The new range in Bering for the unident

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:25.640
puts it almost directly over the submerged intruder.

00:23:34.600 --> 00:23:38.360
A few minutes later, the planes of the carrier's B.S. squadrons are on the scene.

00:23:38.360 --> 00:23:42.840
The sonar are dunking helicopters.

00:23:42.840 --> 00:23:55.860
The hundreds searching fingers of sonar seek the intruder in a sightless world of clicks and beeps and findings.

00:24:01.150 --> 00:24:10.940
In time, he will surface of his own accord, or we will have acquired sufficient useful information about him to permit resumption of the scheduled O.R.E. exercise.

00:24:10.940 --> 00:24:21.940
No single weapon or vehicle can do the total mission of ASW by itself.

00:24:21.940 --> 00:24:26.660
What has been demonstrated is ASW teamwork effectiveness.

00:24:34.440 --> 00:24:37.020
Operations in a Cold War are like shadow boxing.

00:24:37.500 --> 00:24:40.420
No one gets hurt, but one keeps in trim.

00:24:43.610 --> 00:24:49.340
Three ASW groups rotate between our own West Coast and the South China Sea.

00:24:50.310 --> 00:24:56.660
And their job is to maintain constant operational readiness to cope with any submarine threat that might arise.

00:24:56.660 --> 00:25:00.000
That might, as in World War II, threaten American...

00:25:00.030 --> 00:25:09.270
lifelines of merchant shipping or even fire an intercontinental ballistic

00:25:09.270 --> 00:25:15.910
missile in us from beneath the sea. This is one of our own Polaris missiles. We are

00:25:15.910 --> 00:25:23.360
not alone in the technological race. A good way to understand the problem is to

00:25:23.360 --> 00:25:28.070
look at our own submarines. What have they done and what can they do today?

00:25:31.150 --> 00:25:38.280
During World War II, submarines could cruise submerged for only a few hours at very low speeds,

00:25:38.280 --> 00:25:46.930
and they were armed with weapons that had effective ranges measured at best in hundreds of yards.

00:25:46.930 --> 00:25:55.700
These vessels had to surface to charge their batteries and offered a large target for visual or radar sightings.

00:25:55.700 --> 00:26:00.000
Even with these limitations, in World War II, our submarines

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:04.380
accounted for more than 56 percent of all Japanese naval and merchant shipping

00:26:04.380 --> 00:26:14.390
in the Pacific. Snorkeling submarines have the advantage of presenting an

00:26:14.390 --> 00:26:19.890
extremely small target for radar or visual contact, plus the fact that they

00:26:19.890 --> 00:26:24.030
can operate at considerably higher speeds, either snorkeling or submerged,

00:26:24.030 --> 00:26:30.000
which makes them increasingly difficult to attack and destroy. According to

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:37.610
To Jane's fighting ships, the United States has 140 snorkeling submarines of various classes,

00:26:37.610 --> 00:26:46.790
somewhere in the neighborhood of 250 submarines less than the leading submarine power today.

00:26:46.790 --> 00:26:52.330
The nuclear submarine is the first truly submersible vehicle, one that does not have to surface

00:26:52.330 --> 00:27:00.000
at all during a military operation, and yet which has unlimited range, independent of speed.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:08.110
Movements in hull shape have made possible greatly increased submerged cruising speeds.

00:27:08.110 --> 00:27:15.680
The shadow, cast by the glare of nuclear power, is all but uncatchable.

00:27:15.680 --> 00:27:25.180
The leading submarine power in the world today has many of these and is building more.

00:27:25.180 --> 00:27:28.420
Whatever you can do, can someone do it better?

00:27:30.320 --> 00:27:31.780
to assume that they might.

00:27:38.850 --> 00:27:40.830
So that's what ASW is all about.

00:27:41.670 --> 00:27:44.000
A submarine. That silent,

00:27:44.850 --> 00:27:46.310
swift, lethal

00:27:46.310 --> 00:27:48.240
city in a capsule.

00:27:52.630 --> 00:27:54.430
Shadows affecting

00:27:54.430 --> 00:28:00.000
our way of life. Shadows

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:02.570
we must learn to catch.

00:28:02.570 --> 00:28:12.520
A.S.W. Around the Clock.
